        "title": "2. Formal Model, Equations & Protocol Specification Table",
        "content": "To analyze **3.1–3.2 Transport-Layer Services & Multiplexing / Demultiplexing (Connectionless vs. TCP 4-Tuple)** quantitatively, computer networking relies on precise mathematical models, bit-level header specifications, and deterministic state-update equations. The Governing Equation and Architectural Reference Table below summarize the core relationships for **Chapter 3 (Transport Layer (UDP, Reliable Data Transfer rdt, TCP, CUBIC & BBR))**:\n\n$$\\text{EstimatedRTT} = (1-\\alpha)\\,\\text{EstimatedRTT} + \\alpha\\,\\text{SampleRTT}, \\qquad \\text{TimeoutInterval} = \\text{EstimatedRTT} + 4\\,\\text{DevRTT}$$\n\n| Transport Mechanism | Formal Rule / State Variable | Protocol Action & Performance Impact |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **UDP (RFC 768)** | 8-byte header + 16-bit 1's complement checksum | Connectionless, unregulated best-effort segment delivery for DNS, QUIC, and real-time media |\n| **Stop-and-Wait (`rdt3.0`)** | $U_{\\text{sender}} = \\frac{L/R}{\\text{RTT} + L/R}$ | 1-bit alternating sequence number (`0`/`1`) with retransmission timer; low link utilization on high-BDP paths |\n| **Pipelined GBN vs. SR** | Window size $N$; utilization $U = \\min\\left(1, \\frac{N \\cdot L/R}{\\text{RTT} + L/R}\\right)$ | **Go-Back-N** uses cumulative ACKs; **Selective Repeat** buffers out-of-order segments and ACKs individually |\n| **TCP Flow Control** | $\\text{LastByteSent} - \\text{LastByteAcked} \\le \\text{rwnd}$ | Prevents fast sender from overflowing receiver socket buffer (`RcvBuffer` minus unread bytes) |\n| **TCP Slow Start & AIMD** | Double `cwnd` every RTT until `ssthresh`; then $+\\text{MSS}$ per RTT | Multiplicative decrease (`cwnd /= 2`) on 3 Duplicate ACKs (Fast Recovery); reset `cwnd = 1 MSS` on timeout |\n| **TCP CUBIC & BBR** | $W(t) = C(t - K)^3 + W_{\\max}$ (CUBIC) vs. $\\text{BtlBw} \\times \\text{RTprop}$ (BBR) | CUBIC scales window growth independent of RTT; BBR paces at bottleneck bandwidth to avoid bufferbloat |"
